### Title
Win-arm64 upgrade from the launcher-patched release to a canary build.

### Why
The win-arm64 build of conda 26.7.2 (build 1) ships a feedstock-only patch that copies native ARM64 launcher files into conda's own package at build time (AnacondaRecipes/conda-feedstock#94), predating conda's own runtime dependency on `conda-launchers` (#16488). Upgrading that release to a newer build changes how launcher files are sourced; confirm the upgrade does not break existing entry points on native ARM64.

### Platforms
- [x] Windows (win-arm64)
- [ ] macOS
- [ ] Linux

### Prerequisites
- A native win-arm64 Windows 11 machine
- An [experimental version](https://github.com/Anaconda-Sandbox/win-arm64-experimental-installer/releases) of Miniconda win-arm64 installed
- `conda install -n base python>=3.14`
- `conda self update --all`
- A pre-release conda available on `conda-canary/label/dev`.

### Steps
1. On a win-arm64 machine, confirm `conda.exe` and an installed console entry point (e.g. `pip.exe`) run and show as `Arm64` (not `x86` or `x64`) in Task Manager's Architecture column, and that `conda info` reports `platform: win-arm64`.
2. Upgrade conda in place: `conda update -n base -c conda-canary/label/dev conda --yes`.
3. Confirm the upgrade finishes without errors and that `conda-launchers` is now listed in `conda list -n base`.
4. Repeat step 1's checks after the upgrade: `conda.exe` and the same entry point must still run and still show as native `Arm64`, and `conda info` must still report `platform: win-arm64`.
5. Run `conda init` again and confirm activation still works in both PowerShell and cmd.

### Pass criteria
1. The upgrade finishes successfully.
2. Executables such as `conda.exe` and package entry points function afterward and are still reported as `Arm64`, never `x86` or `x64`.
3. `conda info` shows `platform: win-arm64`
4. `conda list -n base` shows `conda-launchers` is installed after the upgrade to the canary version of conda.

### Out of scope / notes
Does not repeat the general x64/ARM64 launcher testing already covered by `16293-conda-launchers`; this snippet only covers the win-arm64 upgrade path from the pre-#16488 feedstock-patched release.
